lets talk about STATEFULSET

Statefulset
==============

lets assume having one application need to be deploy in kubernetes means we will use DEPLOYMENT Object  

its ok while using DEPLOYMENT object and to do deployment to the application in kubernetes 

after deployment done the application will gonna access well, then what about DataBase ?

incase we need to do deploy database means we should not use DEPLOYMENT Onject for Database

we are using STAETEFULSET For database

application will be seperate & database will be seperate

for application purpose we will use DEPLOYMENT Object in kubernetes

for Database purpose we will use STATEFULSET object in kubernetes

what is Statefulset why we should not use deployment ?

in kubernetes we will have 2 types of application

1. STATELESS Application--------------> it means no past data previous data will not be present
Real time example is
lets assueme you deployed your stateless application as a Deployment with 10 Pod replicas running in multiple worker nodes like below

----------------------------------------------->CLUSTER<--------------------------------------------

Node                                    Node                                              Node                            Node

pod  pod                              pod   pod                                        pod   pod                        pod   pod
container container                 container container                               container container              container container

lets assueme you deployed your stateless application as a Deployment with 10 Pod replicas running in multiple worker nodes like above
then, mightbe suddenly mightbedue to network issue or heavy load one pod got deleted, if the pod got deleted means there is no problem again new pod will be get 
created with help of Replicaset

The ReplicaSet controller takes care of replacing the bad Pod with a new healthy Pod either on the same node or on a different node.

Here ReplicaSet's will only take care of those 10 pods are running in the cluster.

It doesn't take care of in which worker node they are running!

HERE IS THE MAIN POINT WE NEED TO BE OBSERVERD IS IN WHICH NODE POD GOT DELETED AND IN WHICH NODE AGAIN NEW POD GET CREATED
=============================================================================================================================

If the pod 1 got terminated from node, then new pod will gets running either node 2 or node1 or anywhere in the cluster

This is possible because, the STATELESS application Pod1 hasn't stored any data on worker node1, hence can be easliy replaced by new pod running on a different 
worker node 2

If the pod is not storing the data then we called it as STATELESS.

